From 42a8c72c72fc67d3c7899c9dc8bc3b1beae5a9cf Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Wed, 28 Oct 2026 20:37:04 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 03/11] physim: LabOracleRunner with an actuator roster apart
 from the observed ports

labworld.LabOracleRunner subclasses blobround6.OracleRunner: inject ports index a declared
actuator roster of (field row, sign) pairs, sample arrays carry every observed port, and
observe-only rows (derived channels such as the flow speed, declared with Derived) cannot be
actuators. It reuses the base constructor checks, _parse, member seeding, devices, pose
updates and sampling, and repeats only the sample_truth scheduler with the actuator count and
the actuator's field and sign. LabWorld gains actuators (Actuator(field, sign)) and derived;
declaration() omits them when undeclared so labeval's frozen suites keep their identity.
ports_check.py shows bit-identity with OracleRunner on phase_membrane and a native Blobkit
world, a finite '-' vorticity actuator on the fed vortices, and an observe-only channel that
the sensors return and the roster rejects. blobround6.py, devices.py and bundles.py are unchanged.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
